WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.099
I'm not waiting around for some damn kid.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:16.620
He's late.

00:00:17.879 --> 00:00:19.240
Your watch is fast.

00:00:20.359 --> 00:00:22.480
You say if there's one thing I am, it's never late.

00:00:22.539 --> 00:00:25.140
I say I'm gonna be somewhere, I'll be there like a flash.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.039
Nice car, man. What is this, real leather?

00:00:28.039 --> 00:00:30.259
I got places to be, small fry.

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:32.000
What do you got for me?

00:00:34.039 --> 00:00:36.079
I got some great stuff here, Mr. Hannison.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.039
I'm talking top of the line.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:52.600
You've been busy.

00:00:53.939 --> 00:00:56.079
You know, you know, idle hands, empty pockets.

00:00:57.179 --> 00:00:57.899
So what do you think?

00:00:58.039 --> 00:01:00.379
I think you're 200 for the lot.

00:01:00.899 --> 00:01:02.379
It's worth like 10 times that much.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:05.359
And I told you I don't handle this nickel-dime crap anymore.

00:01:05.859 --> 00:01:08.019
You land a real score, you come talk to me.

00:01:08.099 --> 00:01:10.039
Until then, you take what I give you.

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:14.659
Maybe. I should just take it all.

00:01:17.859 --> 00:01:19.500
That isn't a threat, is it, kid?

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:34.100
The Woman About Top Gear

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:50.680
I'm looking at the

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:51.800
Wings.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:56.780
.

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:58.519
You don't have to worry your mother with any more of this stuff.

00:01:58.579 --> 00:01:58.920
That's all.

00:02:00.299 --> 00:02:01.659
Dad, we both worry about you.

00:02:03.219 --> 00:02:04.700
What Jarrell did to you because of me.

00:02:04.799 --> 00:02:06.579
Wait a minute. I knew what the risks were, Clark.

00:02:07.299 --> 00:02:08.400
And I'd take them again in a heartbeat

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.460
if it meant keeping you safe.

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:13.120
The two and I have a game to catch.

00:02:14.599 --> 00:02:16.000
Metropolis Sharks, 50-yard line.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:17.740
Lex really came through this time.

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:21.500
Look, son, I understand what that friendship means to you,

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:24.479
but please don't forget he had you investigated.

00:02:24.479 --> 00:02:25.039
Be careful.

00:02:25.159 --> 00:02:26.659
I'm not going into this with my eyes closed.

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:29.080
He wants another chance to prove he's changed.

00:02:30.439 --> 00:02:30.759
Clark.

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:32.560
Dad, this is my senior year.

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:35.439
I don't want to have to worry about Lex or Jarrell or any of that.

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:37.420
I just want to live a normal life,

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:38.759
hang out with my friends and play football.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:41.240
All right, why don't you go get the truck.

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:42.560
We don't want to miss the kickoff.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:59.599
You can tell my dad he'll pay for everything.

00:02:59.659 --> 00:02:59.879
It's...

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:01.039
Store.

00:03:01.699 --> 00:03:03.000
But I don't want to miss the kickoff.

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:09.340
Not on the roof.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:10.120
Take this.

00:03:10.199 --> 00:03:10.819
That is for show.

00:03:10.879 --> 00:03:12.539
Talk to the delivery jaw.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:15.599
That's the worst I've ever had.

00:03:17.039 --> 00:03:19.099
When did you start a career here?

00:03:19.159 --> 00:03:20.099
As favourite actor.

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:25.199
It's an impression of Split enabling children.

00:03:25.319 --> 00:03:26.259
See when they grow up?

00:03:26.259 --> 00:03:26.420
Yeah.

00:03:26.419 --> 00:03:27.659
you had to push me out of the way.

00:03:27.659 --> 00:03:29.199
Dad, it wasn't me.

00:03:29.199 --> 00:03:31.919
I saw someone who can move like I can.

00:03:31.919 --> 00:03:33.639
I couldn't believe it.

00:03:33.639 --> 00:03:34.539
He saved you.

00:03:40.419 --> 00:03:42.319
Whoever it is, not only did he save my life, Clark,

00:03:42.319 --> 00:03:44.119
he also stole my wallet.

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:51.120
Somebody save me.

00:03:57.120 --> 00:04:01.120
Let your wounds break right through.

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:04.120
Somebody save me.

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:11.120
Don't care how you do it.

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:13.120
Just save me.

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:16.120
Stay.

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:18.120
Come on.

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:21.120
I've been waiting for you.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:32.120
I made this whole world shine for you.

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:34.120
Stay.

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:36.120
Stay.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:37.120
Come on.

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:47.120
Stay.

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:03.120
Hey.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:04.620
Aren't you two supposed to be at the game?

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:07.120
Well, the tickets to the game were in my wallet,

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:08.120
which was stolen.

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:10.120
Some kid swiped it outside the medical building.

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:11.120
Oh, my god.

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:12.120
You were robbed?

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:13.120
Are you all right?

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:14.860
a very fast pair of sneakers.

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:17.100
But I'm going to call the credit card company,

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:18.660
report it stolen.

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:20.300
Hey, Dad, wait.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:22.699
This kid, he was as fast as I am.

00:05:22.699 --> 00:05:24.180
I should find out who he is.

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:25.139
Just let me talk to Chloe.

00:05:25.139 --> 00:05:28.939
Maybe she can track down where he's been using your card.

00:05:28.939 --> 00:05:29.840
Come on, Dad.

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:31.379
If I don't find anything by the end of the day,

00:05:31.379 --> 00:05:34.079
then make the call.

00:05:34.079 --> 00:05:35.819
All right, but I want you to be careful, Clark.

00:05:35.819 --> 00:05:37.600
We don't know anything about this kid.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:39.120
That's why I have to find out who he is.

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:44.579
Are you sure you're OK?

00:05:44.579 --> 00:05:45.980
Sweetheart, I'm fine.

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:48.180
I wish you wouldn't worry about me all the time.

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:49.980
You were in a coma for three months, Jonathan.

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:52.439
It's hard not to worry when you've been through so much.

00:05:52.439 --> 00:05:53.680
A little help from modern medicine,

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:56.019
I plan on going through a whole lot more,

00:05:56.019 --> 00:05:59.959
starting with a romantic evening with my beautiful wife.

00:05:59.959 --> 00:06:01.819
Thought maybe we could have a little dinner

00:06:01.819 --> 00:06:03.879
and then drive on down to the lake.

00:06:03.879 --> 00:06:05.000
I'd love that, sweetheart.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:09.199
But I might have to work late again tonight.

00:06:09.199 --> 00:06:11.240
Running the Talon is a lot more involved

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:12.600
than I thought it would be.

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:13.100
But, uh.

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:14.660
I'll call you later, OK?

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:24.939
Head over to the library.

00:06:24.939 --> 00:06:25.939
I need a beer.

00:06:25.939 --> 00:06:26.840
All right.

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:45.060
It's gone now, you dirty.

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:47.140
I'm going to pay for that.

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:48.160
I left my wallet there.

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:49.180
Watch your mouth.

00:06:49.180 --> 00:07:05.280
You're an idiot,

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:09.100
punk.

00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:09.820
Um, thanks a lot.

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:10.580
I appreciate it.

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:11.140
Thanks.

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:11.760
Love you, Laurel.

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:12.360
And you, sir.

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:12.939
You too, Simon.

00:07:12.939 --> 00:07:15.300
before I came back from Paris.

00:07:16.699 --> 00:07:17.100
Really?

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:18.579
Well, why didn't you tell me?

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:22.079
I could have come with you and gotten a mermaid or an anchor

00:07:22.079 --> 00:07:23.500
or a mermaid holding an anchor.

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:24.259
What?

00:07:24.439 --> 00:07:25.779
I didn't plan on getting it, all right?

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:26.639
It kind of just happened.

00:07:27.199 --> 00:07:28.420
Tattoos don't just kind of happen.

00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:32.279
There's usually some ink and a fair amount of paint involved.

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:35.300
Well, what was I supposed to do?

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:37.079
Ask you for permission to get it?

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:38.480
Whoa, hey.

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:40.939
That's not what I meant.

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:42.120
Why are you biting my head off right now?

00:07:42.139 --> 00:07:42.579
I'm not.

00:07:42.579 --> 00:07:43.359
Yes, you are.

00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:45.800
Look, I just...

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:47.919
I don't want you making a big deal out of this.

00:07:50.279 --> 00:07:52.899
I don't care about the tattoo, okay?

00:07:53.839 --> 00:07:57.120
But what bothers me is the fact that, for some weird reason,

00:07:57.180 --> 00:07:58.439
you felt like you had to hide it from me.

00:08:01.759 --> 00:08:04.240
I've seen what keeping secrets has done to my parents.

00:08:04.819 --> 00:08:06.219
I'm not going to end up like that.

00:08:10.439 --> 00:08:12.560
Jason, the last thing I ever want to do

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:13.180
is hurt you.

00:08:14.740 --> 00:08:17.579
But there are some things that I am just...

00:08:17.579 --> 00:08:19.280
I'm not comfortable sharing with you yet.

00:08:22.420 --> 00:08:23.180
I'm sorry.

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:39.899
I'm sorry.

00:08:39.899 --> 00:08:40.639
I'm sorry.

00:08:40.639 --> 00:08:41.240
I'm sorry.

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:41.259
I'm sorry.

00:08:41.259 --> 00:08:41.779
I'm sorry.

00:08:41.779 --> 00:08:41.879
I'm sorry.

00:08:41.879 --> 00:08:41.940
I'm sorry.

00:08:41.940 --> 00:08:42.419
I'm sorry.

00:08:42.419 --> 00:08:42.440
I'm sorry.

00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:42.500
I'm sorry.

00:09:12.559 --> 00:09:42.539
I'm losing it.

00:09:42.559 --> 00:10:12.539
I'm losing it.

00:10:12.559 --> 00:10:42.539
I'm losing it.

00:10:42.559 --> 00:11:12.539
I'm losing it.

00:11:12.559 --> 00:11:12.619
I'm losing it.

00:11:12.619 --> 00:11:12.659
I'm losing it.

00:11:12.659 --> 00:11:12.839
I'm losing it.

00:11:12.839 --> 00:11:13.759
I'm gonna get my dad's wallet,

00:11:13.859 --> 00:11:15.559
then you and I are gonna sit down for a long talk.

00:11:21.639 --> 00:11:22.819
Not big on the chitchat, dude.

00:11:24.199 --> 00:11:24.799
Smiley later.

00:11:42.559 --> 00:12:01.539
Dad, I found the key to Stoia Wallet,

00:12:01.599 --> 00:12:02.819
but I lost it down at the docks.

00:12:03.239 --> 00:12:04.759
He just took off across the water.

00:12:05.459 --> 00:12:06.619
Uh, son.

00:12:06.619 --> 00:12:06.679
Son.

00:12:09.899 --> 00:12:10.459
Hey, Clark.

00:12:12.559 --> 00:12:17.059
What took you so long?

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:28.299
Dude, I didn't think anybody else could move like that except me,

00:12:28.359 --> 00:12:30.079
because, hey, best man alive, right?

00:12:30.759 --> 00:12:31.019
Yeah.

00:12:31.619 --> 00:12:34.299
You were right on my butt, man, and, you know, I've always wondered

00:12:34.299 --> 00:12:35.659
if there was anyone else out there like me,

00:12:35.659 --> 00:12:38.979
and it turns out to be you, Jimmy Crack Corn, fresh from the farm.

00:12:39.279 --> 00:12:40.979
What kind of story did you spin to con my dad

00:12:40.979 --> 00:12:42.500
off a free meal and a bed on the couch?

00:12:42.559 --> 00:12:44.239
No story, Clark, just the truth.

00:12:44.919 --> 00:12:45.579
And what's that?

00:12:46.500 --> 00:12:49.679
All right, well, a couple years ago, there was, like, this accident, right?

00:12:49.739 --> 00:12:50.979
And there was this huge flashlight,

00:12:51.599 --> 00:12:53.739
and then my body went into overdrive.

00:12:54.699 --> 00:12:56.000
And this happened in Smallville?

00:12:57.019 --> 00:12:57.379
No.

00:12:58.239 --> 00:13:01.939
And this is my first time here, and no offense, dude,

00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:04.059
but hopefully the last.

00:13:06.199 --> 00:13:08.139
I've never met anyone with powers like yours

00:13:08.139 --> 00:13:09.239
that wasn't from around here.

00:13:09.719 --> 00:13:12.039
Yeah, well, maybe she'd get out more.

00:13:12.559 --> 00:13:12.879
I don't know.

00:13:14.139 --> 00:13:16.079
So, how'd you get so fast?

00:13:17.619 --> 00:13:19.539
You been acting too, or...?

00:13:19.539 --> 00:13:20.939
Just kind of born this way.

00:13:21.739 --> 00:13:23.019
Why are you living on the streets, Bart?

00:13:26.239 --> 00:13:27.339
What happened to your parents?

00:13:28.539 --> 00:13:30.359
Your son got zapped into a human lightning bolt.

00:13:30.439 --> 00:13:31.119
That's what happened.

00:13:32.119 --> 00:13:33.099
I mean, they made this whole big deal

00:13:33.099 --> 00:13:35.099
that everything was gonna be okay, and that...

00:13:36.919 --> 00:13:39.939
I don't know, man.

00:13:39.939 --> 00:13:41.299
You should have just seen the way they looked at me, huh?

00:13:42.559 --> 00:13:45.319
I could tell that nothing was gonna be the same.

00:13:46.500 --> 00:13:47.399
So you ran away?

00:13:49.119 --> 00:13:49.739
I...

00:13:49.739 --> 00:13:52.559
I just didn't fit in.

00:13:54.079 --> 00:13:55.539
Man, I guess you don't want that problem.

00:13:56.479 --> 00:13:57.559
Oh, you'd be surprised.

00:13:59.519 --> 00:14:00.739
I ran away once, too.

00:14:00.919 --> 00:14:02.019
Yeah, why'd you come back, man?

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:04.379
Mow the lawn? Milk the cows?

00:14:05.239 --> 00:14:06.959
Dude, you should be out there with me, tearing it up.

00:14:07.359 --> 00:14:09.000
You mean stealing everything in sight?

00:14:10.979 --> 00:14:12.519
It's not like I ever really hurt anybody.

00:14:12.559 --> 00:14:15.559
I mean, I usually just swipe a little bling

00:14:15.559 --> 00:14:17.519
from the stiff upper crust whenever I need some cash.

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:20.759
I want you to call a have-not, Clark.

00:14:21.279 --> 00:14:22.299
I take from the haves.

00:14:22.759 --> 00:14:23.500
Like my dad?

00:14:24.739 --> 00:14:25.299
Look, man.

00:14:26.399 --> 00:14:27.419
Don't even sweat it, okay?

00:14:28.039 --> 00:14:29.519
They don't charge you if your card's stolen.

00:14:29.699 --> 00:14:31.099
Oh, and that makes it all right.

00:14:31.819 --> 00:14:32.419
Look, man.

00:14:33.079 --> 00:14:35.559
My fence down in the suicide slums, they sure changed me.

00:14:36.119 --> 00:14:37.959
So I had to boost your dad's card in order to get a room.

00:14:38.019 --> 00:14:39.779
I don't like spending the night out on the streets.

00:14:40.379 --> 00:14:41.500
Okay? Stuff happens there.

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:41.579
Okay.

00:14:42.559 --> 00:14:44.779
When I'm asleep, I'm just as slow as everybody else.

00:14:48.559 --> 00:14:50.399
Don't hit me with the big cow eyes there, Stretch.

00:14:50.879 --> 00:14:52.439
Okay? I could always take care of myself.

00:14:53.079 --> 00:14:54.539
Yeah, you've done a great job so far.

00:14:57.479 --> 00:14:58.239
You know what, man?

00:14:58.259 --> 00:14:59.739
Enough about the poor little street urchin, right?

00:15:00.879 --> 00:15:04.019
Let's take a closer look at the mysterious Clark Kent.

00:15:08.219 --> 00:15:08.779
Let's see.

00:15:08.779 --> 00:15:12.099
You like to read about Native American mythology?

00:15:12.559 --> 00:15:13.059
Yeah.

00:15:13.059 --> 00:15:18.559
You've scrolled the name Lana on all your notebooks.

00:15:18.559 --> 00:15:21.559
And you have one of the most boring hobbies known to man.

00:15:23.559 --> 00:15:24.559
Rock collecting.

00:15:24.559 --> 00:15:25.559
I don't collect rock.

00:15:33.059 --> 00:15:34.059
Dude, are you okay?

00:15:34.059 --> 00:15:35.059
Get that away.

00:15:36.059 --> 00:15:37.059
I'm allergic.

00:15:39.559 --> 00:15:42.559
Man, I've heard of people sneezing around cats and dogs,

00:15:42.559 --> 00:15:45.059
and stuff, and never getting all weak, and the knee is over a rock.

00:15:45.059 --> 00:15:46.059
It's a long story.

00:15:47.559 --> 00:15:49.559
Which is one I'm sure I would love to hear.

00:15:49.559 --> 00:15:50.559
After we get back.

00:15:52.059 --> 00:15:53.559
Get back from where?

00:15:53.559 --> 00:15:54.559
Anywhere we want.

00:15:55.559 --> 00:15:57.559
I mean, dude, we are two super-powered studs here.

00:15:58.559 --> 00:16:00.559
Why else do you think I came to Smellyville looking for you, man?

00:16:00.559 --> 00:16:02.559
Let's go crank it up. Go have some fun.

00:16:03.559 --> 00:16:04.559
You ever seen Florida?

00:16:12.559 --> 00:16:13.559
Yes.

00:16:17.559 --> 00:16:20.559
Dude, man, that girl on the black bikini, she was totally checking you out.

00:16:20.559 --> 00:16:21.559
No, she wasn't.

00:16:21.559 --> 00:16:24.559
Look, the girl was eyeing you like you were a snow cone, dude.

00:16:24.559 --> 00:16:25.559
You should've gotten her number.

00:16:25.559 --> 00:16:27.559
I can't just walk up to a girl on the beach and get her phone number.

00:16:27.559 --> 00:16:31.559
Yeah, well, lucky for you, I can.

00:16:32.559 --> 00:16:34.559
You should have to call her next time you're in Miami.

00:16:34.559 --> 00:16:35.559
What? Shh.

00:16:35.559 --> 00:16:37.559
I can't just go run back down to Miami.

00:16:37.559 --> 00:16:38.559
Why not?

00:16:38.559 --> 00:16:40.559
Because it's, it's what?

00:16:40.559 --> 00:16:41.559
Too much fun, Clark?

00:16:41.559 --> 00:16:43.559
Come on, dude, nobody's ever died from it.

00:16:46.559 --> 00:16:47.559
What are you doing?

00:16:48.559 --> 00:16:50.559
I'm eating a cookie, dude. I'm starving.

00:16:50.559 --> 00:16:52.559
You can't just take whatever you want.

00:16:52.559 --> 00:16:53.559
Mom runs this place.

00:16:53.559 --> 00:16:55.559
Look, man, there's a line.

00:16:56.559 --> 00:16:57.559
I don't do lines.

00:16:57.559 --> 00:16:58.559
What's up, Kent?

